  "output": "We are given: \"John has 10 hectares of a pineapple field. There are 100 pineapples per hectare. John can harvest his pineapples every 3 months. How many pineapples can John harvest within a year?\"\n\nWe need to solve step by step and end with FINAL: <integer>.\n\nLet's break it down:\n\n- Area: 10 hectares.\n- Pineapples per hectare: 100.\n- So total pineapples in the field: 10 * 100 = 1000 pineapples.\n- Harvesting frequency: every 3 months.\n- Within a year: 12 months.\n- Number of harvests per year: 12 months / 3 months per harvest = 4 harvests per year.\n- Total pineapples harvested: 1000 * 4 = 4000.\n\nSo answer is 4000.\n\nCheck: 10 ha * 100 = 1000. 12 months / 3 = 4. 1000 * 4 = 4000.\n\nThus final answer: 4000.</think>John has 10 hectares of pineapple field, with 100 pineapples per hectare. Total pineapples = 10 × 100 = 1000. He harvests every 3 months, so in a year (12 months) he harvests 12 ÷ 3 = 4 times. Total harvested = 1000 × 4 = 4000.\n\nFINAL: 4000",
